1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0281-985cd8228d12:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 342, \"text\": \"The Donner Party (1992 film) The Donner Party is a 1992 documentary film that traces the history of the Donner Party, an ill-fated pioneer group that trekked from Springfield, Illinois to Sutter's Fort, California - a disastrous journey of 2500 miles made famous by the tales of cannibalism the survivors told upon reaching their destination.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0281-985cd8228d12:d00\", \"start\": 343, \"end\": 535, \"text\": \"The film, narrated by David McCullough, premiered at the Telluride Mountainfilm Festival in May 1992 with an introductory lecture on the Donner Party by noted Western historian David Lavender.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0281-985cd8228d12:d00\", \"start\": 536, \"end\": 627, \"text\": \"It subsequently aired on PBS as part of the \\\"American Experience\\\" program in October, 1992.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0281-985cd8228d12:d00\", \"start\": 628, \"end\": 631, \"text\": \"The\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0281-985cd8228d12:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 70, \"text\": \"Troublesome Creek : A Midwestern Truman Two Days in October Ulysses S.\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0281-985cd8228d12:d01\", \"start\": 71, \"end\": 276, \"text\": \"Grant Vietnam : A Television History Walt Disney We Shall Remain Wild by Law Woodrow Wilson and the Birth of the American Century The Wright Stuff Retrieved from `` https : //en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php ?\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0281-985cd8228d12:d01\", \"start\": 277, \"end\": 713, \"text\": \"title=The_Donner_Party_ ( 1992_film ) & oldid=1244241936 `` Categories : 1992 films American Experience Television series by WNET American documentary films Films directed by Ric Burns 1992 documentary films Documentary films about California Donner Party 1990s English-language films 1990s American films English-language documentary films Hidden categories : Articles with short description Short description matches Wikidata Template\"}, \"D3S1\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0281-985cd8228d12:d02\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 131, \"text\": \"The Donner Party (2009 film) The Donner Party is a 2009 period drama film written and directed by Terrence Martin (credited as T.J.\"}, \"D3S2\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0281-985cd8228d12:d02\", \"start\": 132, \"end\": 246, \"text\": \"Martin), and starring Crispin Glover, Clayne Crawford, Michele Santopietro, Mark Boone Junior, and Christian Kane.\"}, \"D3S3\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0281-985cd8228d12:d02\", \"start\": 247, \"end\": 366, \"text\": \"It is based on the true story of the Donner Party, an 1840s westward traveling group of settlers headed for California.\"}, \"D3S4\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0281-985cd8228d12:d02\", \"start\": 367, \"end\": 523, \"text\": \"Becoming snowbound in the Sierra Nevada mountains, with food increasingly scarce, a small group calling themselves \\\"The Forlorn Hope\\\" turned to cannibalism.\"}, \"D3S5\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0281-985cd8228d12:d02\", \"start\": 524, \"end\": 573, \"text\": \"\\\"The Forlorn\\\" was the working title for the film.\"}, \"D3S6\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0281-985cd8228d12:d02\", \"start\": 574, \"end\": 630, \"text\": \"The film opens with text explaining who the Donner Party\"}, \"D4S1\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0281-985cd8228d12:d03\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 66, \"text\": \"the banishment of James Reed , the Donner Party was coming apart .\"}, \"D4S2\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0281-985cd8228d12:d03\", \"start\": 67, \"end\": 165, \"text\": \"On October 7th , Lewis Keseberg turned an aging Belgian emigrant named Hardkoop out of his wagon .\"}, \"D4S3\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0281-985cd8228d12:d03\", \"start\": 166, \"end\": 197, \"text\": \"No one else would take him in .\"}, \"D4S4\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0281-985cd8228d12:d03\", \"start\": 198, \"end\": 297, \"text\": \"The old man fell farther and father behind and was last seen sitting by the road , unable to walk .\"}, \"D4S5\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0281-985cd8228d12:d03\", \"start\": 298, \"end\": 381, \"text\": \"On the night of October 12th , Paiute Indians killed 21 oxen with poisoned arrows .\"}, \"D4S6\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0281-985cd8228d12:d03\", \"start\": 382, \"end\": 437, \"text\": \"The company had now lost more than 100 head of cattle .\"}, \"D4S7\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0281-985cd8228d12:d03\", \"start\": 438, \"end\": 499, \"text\": \"From the bluffs above the river , they could hear the Paiutes\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0281-985cd8228d12:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0281-985cd8228d12:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"The film about the Donner Party\", \"scope\": \"format\", \"claim\": \"The format of the film about the Donner Party is a documentary.\", \"answer\": \"documentary\", \"quote\": \"The Donner Party (1992 film) The Donner Party is a 1992 documentary film that traces the history of the Donner Party, an ill-fated pioneer group that trekked from Springfield, Illinois to Sutter's Fort, California - a disastrous journey of 2500 miles made famous by the tales of cannibalism the survivors told upon reaching their destination.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0281-985cd8228d12:d01\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0281-985cd8228d12:d01:c0\", \"entity\": \"film about the Donner Party\", \"scope\": \"format\", \"claim\": \"The format of the film about the Donner Party is a documentary film.\", \"answer\": \"d